<h2 id="a-whole-program">A whole program</h2>

<p>This is the code of <a href="https://github.com/anistark/waspy/blob/main/examples/shopping_cart.py"><code>examples/shopping_cart.py</code></a> from the repository, as it is apart from its module docstring. Nothing in it was chosen to show off a compiler feature, and its results are asserted against what CPython answers for the same source, under three WebAssembly runtimes.</p>

<div class="not-prose my-6 code-window">
    <div class="code-window-bar">
        <div class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <span>shopping_cart.py</span>
    </div>
{% highlight "python" %}
class Item:
    def __init__(self, name: str, price: float, qty: int):
        self.name = name
        self.price = price
        self.qty = qty

    def subtotal(self) -> float:
        return self.price * self.qty


class Cart:
    def __init__(self):
        self.items = []
        self.count = 0

    def add(self, name: str, price: float, qty: int):
        item = Item(name, price, qty)
        self.items.append(item)
        self.count = self.count + 1

    def total(self) -> float:
        out: float = 0.0
        for it in self.items:
            out = out + it.subtotal()
        return out

    def units(self) -> int:
        n: int = 0
        for it in self.items:
            n = n + it.qty
        return n


def discount_rate(total: float) -> float:
    if total >= 100.0:
        return 0.10
    if total >= 50.0:
        return 0.05
    return 0.0


def checkout() -> float:
    cart = Cart()
    cart.add("widget", 9.99, 3)
    cart.add("gadget", 24.50, 2)
    cart.add("doohickey", 5.00, 4)
    subtotal = cart.total()
    rate = discount_rate(subtotal)
    return subtotal - subtotal * rate


def item_count() -> int:
    cart = Cart()
    cart.add("a", 1.0, 2)
    cart.add("b", 2.0, 3)
    return cart.count * 100 + cart.units()


def empty_cart_total() -> float:
    cart = Cart()
    return cart.total()
{% endhighlight %}
</div>

<p>Compiled, every function above is an export a host can call: <code>checkout()</code> answers <code>94.0215</code>, <code>item_count()</code> answers <code>205</code>, and <code>empty_cart_total()</code> answers <code>0.0</code>, as CPython does. What you need to know to write the same:</p>

<div class="not-prose glass my-6 p-5 sm:p-6 {{ codecls }}">
    <dl class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-5 sm:grid-cols-[8.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber uppercase sm:pt-0.5">Annotations</dt>
        <dd class="-mt-3.5 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-1 sm:mt-0">Parameter and return annotations pick the WebAssembly value types. A collection passed into or out of a function needs the parameterised form, <code>List[str]</code> rather than a bare <code>list</code>: the parameterised form is what gives the compiler an element type. Calls may pass arguments by keyword, and functions and <code>__init__</code> collect extras with <code>*args: T</code> and <code>**kwargs: T</code>.</dd>

        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber uppercase sm:pt-0.5">Entry points</dt>
        <dd class="-mt-3.5 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-1 sm:mt-0">Every module-level <code>def</code> is exported. There is no top-level run step, so module level holds definitions only; put the code that runs in a function, or under <code>if __name__ == "__main__":</code>, which makes the module a WASI command that <code>wasmtime run</code> runs like <code>python3</code>.</dd>

        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber uppercase sm:pt-0.5">Imports</dt>
        <dd class="-mt-3.5 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-1 sm:mt-0"><code>import mod</code> and <code>from mod import f</code> resolve sibling <code>.py</code> files (and <code>pkg/mod.py</code> packages) from disk and link them into the one output module, each compiled once. No PyPI packages: beyond your own modules, the supported subset is standard-library only.</dd>

        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber uppercase sm:pt-0.5">Side effects</dt>
        <dd class="-mt-3.5 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-1 sm:mt-0"><code>print()</code>, <code>input()</code>, <code>sys.argv</code>, and <code>open()</code> go through WASI, and a module imports only the WASI functions it uses, so the program above imports nothing at all. See <a class="link" href="/docs/running/">Running compiled modules</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
</div>

